  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "n-p1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -320,
      "w": 1600,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "PUBLIC SITE \u2014 THE WHOLE SECTION\nEleven screens on desktop, eleven at 390px below.\nLanding \u00b7 About \u00b7 Events \u00b7 One event \u00b7 Gallery \u00b7 One album \u00b7 Projects \u00b7 One project \u00b7 Opportunities \u00b7 News \u00b7 Verify\n\nPhotographs and video run through all of it. Every album is attached to the event, project or competition it came from,\nso a picture always leads back to the programme, the date and who took part \u2014 the archive is the proof, not decoration."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p1b",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -130,
      "w": 1600,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Media tiles are deliberate placeholders, not grey boxes: a grid of them reads as 'photographs go here'. Swap in real files when there are some.\nVerify is the one screen a stranger judges the whole branch by \u2014 an employer with a code and no account \u2014 so it is plain, document-like, and answers the only question they have in the first line."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 1200,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "JOINING\nSign up, the wrong-address and expired-link states, sign in, and the shareable quick-join link.\nFour fields, no password anywhere in this section."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 1400,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "MEMBER AREA\nNine screens both viewports, the two onboarding states, and the component sheet.\nThe rule running through it: the member never maintains their own record."
    },
    {
      "id": "n-p4",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -260,
      "w": 1500,
      "page": "page-4",
      "text": "EXECUTIVE AREA\nTwelve screens on desktop, ten at 390px.\nEvery screen leads with what is waiting on the executive, and the expensive jobs are one action for a whole batch.\nAttendance works with no network, because if it fails at the hall door everything downstream has nothing to be built from."
    }
  ],
